# [Interactive Active Directory New User Creation Script]
Date: [08/2026]
Status: [completed]

---

## Overview
this is a PowerShell script built for the homelab AD environment that automates the process of creating new Active Directory users through an interactive, looping prompt. 
instead of manually running New-ADUser for every account, the script asks for first name, last name, username, department, and title, maps the user to the correct OU based on department, 
optionally creates/adds them to a department security group, and verifies the account was created correctly — all in one continuous session so multiple users can be created back to back without re-running the script.

---

## Environment
- Device: [Windows Server 2025 DC]
- OS: [Windows Server 2025]
- Domain: [homelab.local]
- Tooling: [PowerShell 5.1, ActiveDirectory module]
---
## Steps
1. [imported the ActiveDirectory module and pulled the domain's DNS root and distinguished name dynamically with Get-ADDomain, so the script isn't hardcoded to one domain]
2. [built a do/while loop so the whole account creation process repeats until the admin chooses not to create another user]
3. [prompted for first name, last name, SAM account name, department, and title, with a check that required fields aren't left blank]
4. [added a duplicate check with Get-ADUser -Filter before going any further, so the script doesn't attempt to create an account that already exists]
5. [built a switch statement to map department to the correct OU using the domain's base DN, so IT/HR/Sales/default all land in the right place automatically]
6. [prompted for a password twice using Read-Host -AsSecureString so the password is masked on screen instead of echoed in plaintext, then converted both SecureStrings to BSTR just long enough to compare them 
   for a match, and zeroed the BSTR pointers right after]
7. [wrapped the group creation, New-ADUser call, and group membership add all in the same try/catch/finally block, with -ErrorAction Stop on each so any failure is caught in one place instead of crashing the loop]
8. [used a finally block to null out the password variable after every iteration so it doesn't sit in memory longer than it needs to]
9. [ran Get-ADUser with -Properties Department, Title, MemberOf after creation to print a verification summary confirming the account, OU, department, title, and group membership]

