## Notes
manually creating AD accounts one at a time through ADUC gets repetitive fast, and doing it by hand increases the chance of typos in UPNs, wrong OU placement, or inconsistent naming. I wanted a script that handles 
the repetitive parts (OU routing, group assignment, verification) while still prompting for the info that actually needs a human decision. also wanted to build something that reflects real 
sysadmin/help desk workflow — onboarding automation is a common ask in entry-level IT roles, so this doubles as a practical skill demo and a portfolio piece.

went through several security-focused revisions on the password handling specifically: the first draft used Read-Host with -AsSecureString:$false, which echoes the password in plaintext on screen 
as it's typed. reworked it to use proper SecureString input for both the password and confirmation, and only converted to plaintext briefly (via BSTR) to check that the two entries matched, immediately 
zeroing that memory afterward. also moved from hardcoded OU distinguished names to building them off the domain's actual base DN via Get-ADDomain, so the script isn't tied to one hardcoded domain if reused elsewhere.

